Amy stands behind her wooden bar in a tunic and apron that billow around her knees, holding a mug of ale in one hand as she looks straight at the camera.

She pushes open the heavy oak door with a firm pull on its iron handle, letting a group of goblins and elves step inside. The door creaks shut behind them.

Amy lifts each goblin’s mug from the barrel, pouring golden ale into it, then hands an elf a crystal glass filled with sparkling wine; she nods to each creature as they sip their drinks.

She takes a cloth in her hand, wipes down a wooden table that has been used by several customers, and places fresh plates of stew and polished goblets on the clean surface.

A dragon perched in the corner lifts its head, tail flicking. Amy offers it a bowl of steaming stew; the dragon licks the bowl with its long tongue.

She grabs a rag, wipes the bar counter until it shines, then pushes the door closed behind her as she turns to face the camera one last time.
